---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

import scoville1 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville1.png';
import scoville2 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville2.png';
import scoville3 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville3.png';
import scoville4 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville4.png';
import scoville5 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville5.png';
import scoville6 from '../../assets/images/projects/scoville/scoville6.png';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Scoville - Artem Androsov"
  description="Scoville — packaging design for a spicy ice cream product on Samokat. Two full designs in two weeks."
  ogImage="/og/scoville.jpg"
  activePage="projects"
>
        <div class="back-nav">
            <a href="/" class="back-link">Back to projects</a>
        </div>

        <section class="project-hero" id="hero">
            <div class="section-label">Case study</div>
            <h1>Scoville</h1>
            <p class="project-brief">A spicy ice cream for a major express delivery platform — designed twice. The first
                version was ready, approved, and killed by the retailer. The second had to be built from near-zero in
                days, without losing the product's character in the process.</p>

            <div class="project-meta">
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">Date</span>
                    <span class="meta-value">February 2026</span>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">My role</span>
                    <span class="meta-value">Product, Packaging Design</span>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">Areas</span>
                    <div class="meta-tags">
                        <span class="meta-tag">Packaging Design</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Visual Concept</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Retail</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-concept" id="concept">
            <div class="www-grid">
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">Why</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">Scoville — a sauce brand known for heat — decided to enter the ice cream
                        category with a provocative product: vanilla ice cream with spicy pomegranate topping. The
                        distribution target was Samokat, one of the largest express delivery platforms in the market. The brief
                        was clear: packaging that earns shelf space and communicates the contradiction at the heart of
                        the product — cold and spicy, delicate and aggressive.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">What</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">We researched the category thoroughly before touching any design tool — online references and physical store visits, mapping every existing ice cream format on the market. The first version was built around a central character: a stylised cartoon illustration that anchored the entire visual concept. When the initial concept was rejected due to external partnership constraints, the design lost its central anchor. Not just a face — the entire visual hierarchy had to be rebuilt. What stays, what becomes the new anchor, what communicates the brand's edge without the character it was built around. We solved it. The final packaging went to production, hit Samokat's catalogue, and is selling.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">How</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">The pivot was the real design challenge. Starting over isn't the hard part —
                        starting over while keeping the product's personality intact is. The spicy-cold tension that
                        defined the first version still had to read in the second, just through different means. I
                        directed the redesign from a high-level perspective: reviewing at every step, identifying what worked and
                        what didn't, keeping the energy of the original concept alive in a completely different
                        execution. Two weeks total — one for the version that didn't ship, one for the version that did.
                        The constraint didn't weaken the result. It sharpened it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-gallery" id="gallery">
            <div class="section-label">Process &amp; outcome</div>
            <h2>What it looks like</h2>

            <div class="gallery-grid">
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville1} alt="Scoville — image 1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville2} alt="Scoville — image 2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville3} alt="Scoville — image 3" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville4} alt="Scoville — image 4" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville5} alt="Scoville — image 5" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={scoville6} alt="Scoville — image 6" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-results" id="results">
            <div class="section-label">Results</div>
            <h2>What we delivered</h2>

            <div class="metrics-grid">
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">2</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Full designs</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">One killed mid-process, one shipped — both built from scratch</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">2 weeks</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Total timeline</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Including full pivot and rebuild after retailer rejection</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">Live</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">On Samokat</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Spicy vanilla ice cream available now on one of the largest express delivery platforms — retail link below</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">1</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Core tension</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Cold and spicy — had to survive a complete visual overhaul</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-shipped" id="shipped">
            <div class="section-label">What shipped</div>
            <p class="shipped-text">The packaging shipped in early February 2026 and is currently selling on Samokat — one of the largest express delivery platforms in the market. The cold + spicy product tension survived the visual overhaul: the new design carries the same energy through different means.</p>
            <a href="https://samokat.ru/product/morozhenoe-scoville-vanilnyy-plombir-s-ostrym-toppingom-so-vkusom-granata-90-g" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 500;">View product on Samokat →</a>
        </section>

        <section class="next-project" id="next">
            <div class="section-label">Next project</div>
            <a href="/projects/viril" class="next-project-link">
                <span class="next-project-name">Viril</span>
                <span class="next-project-arrow">→</span>
            </a>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-section" id="cta">
            <h2>Need packaging that stands out?</h2>
            <p class="contact-subtitle contact-subtitle-margin">
                Tell me about the product — I'll find its visual voice.
            </p>
            <a href="https://cal.com/artemandrosov/intro" target="_blank" class="btn-primary" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book an intro call</a>
            <p style="margin-top: 14px; font-size: 0.875rem; opacity: 0.7;">or email <a href="mailto:art.androsov@gmail.com" style="color: inherit;">art.androsov@gmail.com</a></p>
        </section>

        <Footer />
</ProjectLayout>
